      "posterArt": "Figma DqlTNiJFPwa7l5EHTR6qoO 163:2 'Frame 13' — per-poster geometry lifted from each node (was apps/awanaija/src/lib/presidential-2027.ts)",
      "profiles": "Figma 1:987 (APC) / 1:1209 (NDC) — editorial copy; career/education deliberately NOT here (they join on the official record)"
    },
    "images": "Every image key is relative to CDN_BASE_URL (https://cdn.ournigeria.ng). All 39 objects already exist in S3 under election/2027/presidential/… and parties/…; the script uploads nothing. apps/awanaija/public/presidential/ duplicates these and can be deleted once the pages read from the API.",
    "posterArt": "Coordinates are in the 404x695 poster space. bg = the poster's own fill (NOT PoliticalParty.color) → campaigns.brand_color. candidate/mate boxes, chip, scrim, urlColor → campaign_media.metadata on the poster_candidate / poster_mate rows.",
    "order": "The order of `tickets` IS the landing-page rail order (campaigns.display_order = position, first = 1) — Figma 163:2 left to right. To reorder, move the entry and re-run the seed; there is no per-ticket override, and the DB rejects two tickets on one rank within a race.",
    "openQuestions": [
      "APM running mate: the board names Ibrahim Adamu Bala (Bauchi) per westafricanpilotnews; the poster fixture said 'Bala Mohammed' and the S3 key is apm/bala-mohammed/hero.webp. The board is used; confirm the photo is the right person.",
      "NDP vs NRM running mates: the board (INEC list) gives NDP = Samuel Magdalene Gali and NRM = unclear; the Figma posters read 'Ada & Chikwuemeka' (NDP) and 'Okereke & Gali' (NRM). The board is used; NRM mate left null; both tickets at confidence medium.",
      "YPP 'Egbeola', AAC 'Magashi', ADP 'Chinazam' are surname-only from the posters — no source names them in full. Kept at confidence low.",
      "The APC and NDC manifesto covers are the 2023 documents (Figma placeholders); pageCount 80 is the design's '1 of 80', not a real count.",
      "APP has no logo in S3 (the fixture reused NRM's). Left null so the party's own logo_url is used."
    ]
